# Compiled binaries. `go build` in the repository root leaves one named after
# the module, and `git add -A` sweeps it in. Build to /tmp instead.
/smb
/cover.out
# …and the command's own build output, which `go build ./...` inside its
# directory leaves next to the source.
#
# Named rules do not work here, and this file has the proof: the rule used to
# say /cmd/smb-server/smb-server, and a 6.5 MB `smbserve` -- the binary of the
# name the command had BEFORE -- was committed by the same change that did the
# rename. So this is an allow-list instead: inside a command's directory,
# nothing is committed unless it is source. A binary cannot slip in under a
# name nobody thought of, whichever direction the rename goes.
/cmd/*/*
!/cmd/*/*.go
!/cmd/*/*.hcl
!/cmd/*/*.md
!/cmd/*/go.mod
!/cmd/*/go.sum
!/cmd/*/testdata/
